# ---- 2026-08-09 EXPANSION: 9 -> 21 rows, so `route` clears MIN_SCORABLE_ROWS = 20 ----
# LABELLING RULE, stated so the ground truth is auditable rather than my opinion:
#   The eval feeds the worker TITLE + DESCRIPTION ONLY. If I labelled from that same text, the eval
#   would measure agreement-with-me, not correctness. So every row below is labelled from a field
#   the worker CANNOT see:
#     TIER 1 (structural, strongest) — issue_type:
#         Incident Ticket / PagerDuty        -> rca   (an operational incident is investigated)
#         Feature                            -> coding (a feature is built)
#     TIER 2 — issue_type Query whose summary explicitly asks to investigate -> rca
#     TIER 3 (weakest, used for 2 rows, flagged inline) — Task whose summary names an unambiguous
#         code action (Fix / Revert). This one DOES read the prose; treated as the least reliable.
#   SKIPPED deliberately: tickets where the tiers disagree (MM-14245 is typed PagerDuty but its
#   summary is a backend migration), and the MM-14378 ai-spec siblings that are ops/config rather
#   than code (create a company + API key, ELD config, env-config enrollment, share a contract).
#   `domain_bucket` is left "" on every new row -- unverified, so route-only scoring, per this
#   file's own rule that a wrong label poisons the eval worse than an unscored one.
#
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-09 (read the resolutions, read-only): MM-14627 and MM-14825 RE-LABELLED
#   rca -> coding. The Tier-1 structural rule (Incident Ticket / PagerDuty -> rca) was WRONG on both,
#   and the router was right both times:
#     MM-14627 resolution comment: "The issue has been FIXED by adding the tracking ids to the REDIS.
#              The RCA will be done as part of MM-14462" -- the fix landed HERE, the RCA was split out.
#     MM-14825 description IS a finished RCA (root cause pinned to two code defects: the logger's Hash
#              assumption, and the rdkafka adapter missing `headers:`), so what remained was the fix.
#   LESSON FOR THIS FILE: issue_type is weaker ground truth than the RESOLUTION. An operational
#   incident whose fix is applied in-ticket is a `coding` row. Prefer the resolution where it exists.
# PER-ROW EVIDENCE (the field the label came from):
